We first traverse the quasi-adjacent vertices of \(v_1\) to obtain \(X_1\). 
Then, for each vertex in \(X_1\), we successively find all of its quasi-adjacent vertices that are closest to it, 
whose union forms \(X_2\).
Similarly, for each vertex in \(X_2\), we obtain all its quasi-adjacent vertices, 
whose union forms \(X_3\), and so on (see Fig.\ref{2-8-4}). 
This process continues iteratively until all vertices in \(X\) have been traversed. At each iteration, the corresponding operations are performed according to the four cases (Case 1–Case 4). As a result, we obtain \(d_T(v_{t_i}, v_{t_{i+1}}) \leq 2(i=1,2,\dots,k)\) for \(v_{t_i} \in X_i\) and \(v_{t_{i+1}} \in X_{i+1}\) with \(v_{t_i} \dot{\sim} v_{t_{i+1}}\). 
